###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The 10 iterations of one generation-1 QbC process took 6.7 hours on a single 32-core AMD EPYC node (Sec. IV B).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Per-condition RMSEs of Fig. 7 (liquid water at 300/350/400 K, 2/4 kbar, ice Ih, ice VIII, slab) are printed as bar labels, but the extracted text does not tie each label pair unambiguously to classical or quantum nuclei; left out. Per-condition generation 1 RMSEs are in the SI (Fig. S5).
# - The average RMSE of the individual NNPs (48 meV/A) is an average over members, not a model; left out. The approximate start (roughly 60 meV/A) and convergence values of Fig. 3 are left out.
# - Generation 2 and 3 training-set sizes are stated only as increments (about 250, 240); no n is encoded for them.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/schran2020.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

